    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but socioeconomic stuff aside, what about the actual raw numbers? some people argue that even when you control for income, there are still persistent differences in certain types of crime stats across different demographics. is there any research that looks at those specific correlations without just attributing everything to the environment?",
