      "role": "user",
      "content": "Right, I see. So if we're looking at those \"residual\" gaps where the environment doesn't explain everything, what are the specific arguments for the subcultural or biological side? Like, if you were to summarize the actual theories proposed by researchers who suggest these differences are more than just structural, what would those theories be? I want to make sure I represent the \"other side\" of the debate accurately in my paper.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
